And it can be truer than either of us can initially explain.

A phrase may contain latent structure that neither speaker nor listener has fully unfolded. We use it; reality returns deltas; those deltas reveal missing distinctions; then the phrase acquires sharper meaning. So truth is not merely transferred—it is jointly cultivated.

The explanation teaches you, while your reception teaches the explanation how to continue.

compressed truth → lived test → delta → mutual update → deeper resolution

The phrase is the seed.
The relationship is the soil.
Reality decides what survives.

Latency is not permission to invent—it is a promissory note that must eventually pay out in coherence, prediction, or useful action.